From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Open Arc Authors <dev@openarc.invalid>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:53:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] openarc: chrome: let an embedder confirm extension installs
 and list its tabs

Open Arc embeds Chrome's browser process and shows its tabs in its own UI,
without Browser windows (chrome::EmbedderOwnsUI()). Chrome's extension
system works there, but three of its UI assumptions do not hold:

- ExtensionInstallPrompt shows its confirmation with a Views dialog parented
  to a Browser window. Adds ExtensionInstallPrompt::
  SetEmbedderShowDialogCallback(): when set, every prompt runs the embedder's
  callback instead of its dialog (the embedder draws the confirmation and runs
  the DoneCallback). The Web Store's "Add to Chrome" flow and
  WebstoreInstallWithPrompt go through it.
- ExtensionInstallUIDesktop::OnInstallSuccess() shows the "added" bubble in
  a Browser window and creates one when none exists; under an embedder-owned
  UI it now does nothing (the embedder learns about the extension from the
  ExtensionRegistry).
- chrome.tabs.query() lists the tab strips of Browser windows only, so an
  extension popup asking for {active: true, currentWindow: true} finds no
  tab. Adds ExtensionTabUtil::SetEmbedderTabList(): the embedder's tabs with
  whether each is shown and in the current window; TabsQueryFunction appends
  them when the query names no window id, index or window type (they have no
  window and no index, like the tabs of patch 0019's lookup).

Nothing changes when no embedder registers a callback (Chrome never does).
Needed by plan task C14 (extensions). There is no upstream embedding hook
for any of these.
